<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			15/5/97		   7/5/97	     17/5/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	575-600		  625-650	     400-425</p>
<p>    Naphtha	  75-100			125		 50-75</p>
<p>    Gas oil	   1,650		    1,700		 1,525</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	400-425		  350-375	     375-400</p>
<p>    Jet kero	  10-15			 10		 20-25</p>
<p>Gasoline stock movements were fairly brisk with material going transatlantic and into Germany.</p>
<p>Naphtha stocks dipped as product left for the gasoline pool and to the chemical sector.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks were down despite cargo arrivals from Russia. Product departed down the Rhine and into France.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks rose despite some utility demand and German buying of vacuum gas oil.</p>
<p>Jet fuel inventories were slightly higher.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom, +31 20 504 5004</p>
